The refactor tool is not available, so I cannot add a seam to inject the logger. Instead, I will write the test without mocking the logger factory. I will create a real LoggerFactory instance and use it to create the WaitingGroupState. The test will verify the state changes and not verify the logger calls directly, since the logger is not mockable in this context.

I will submit the revised tests now. They will cover the call to LogDebug indirectly by exercising the code path that triggers it.

